{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_37","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\WINDOWS\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command '$f='\"'verdicts\\\\lane3_ltx_video.md'; \\\"===== \"'$f =====\"; if(-not(Test-Path -LiteralPath $f)){ \"MISSING\"; exit 0 }; $lines=Get-Content -LiteralPath $f; for($i=1; ($i -le 300) -and ($i -le $lines.Count); $i++){ '\"'{0,5}: {1}' -f \"'$i,$lines[$i-1] }'","aggregated_output":"===== verdicts\\lane3_ltx_video.md =====\r\n    1: # Lane 3 verdict -- `ltx_video` distilled LoRA strength, ours (0.7) vs half (0.5)\r\n    2: \r\n    3: **RESULT: NO WIN. The shipped `_LTX_DISTILLED_LORA_STRENGTH = 0.70` stands.\r\n    4: Nothing is queued as an OTR item.** Decided by the matrix pre-declared in\r\n    5: `LANE.json` before any render: no structural-regression dominance either way,\r\n    6: no material gain for the candidate = null at the shipping output.\r\n    7: \r\n    8: ## The knob and its bound\r\n    9: \r\n   10: ONE literal: `lora.strength_model` on `LoraLoaderModelOnly`, 0.7 shipped vs\r\n   11: 0.5, SAME LoRA file both arms (`ltx-2.3-22b-distilled-lora-384-1.1`). The\r\n   12: official template pairs 0.5 with the download-gated rank-111 dynamic LoRA that\r\n   13: is not on disk, so the candidate arm is named `half`, never `official` -- this\r\n   14: lane says nothing about the official file+strength combination.\r\n   15: \r\n   16: ## What was run\r\n   17: \r\n   18: Three t2v prompt-fixtures (portrait / march / radio -- prompts ARE the\r\n   19: fixtures on a text-to-video lane) x 2 arms x 2 seeds = 12 legs, all success,\r\n   20: 97 frames at 1024x576, 100-120s per leg. Purity: changed set exactly\r\n   21: `{lora.strength_model}` on the STAGED graphs; on the SUBMITTED graphs it is\r\n   22: that knob **plus the output destination** (`save.filename_prefix`), which\r\n   23: `render_arms.py` declares to the gate and which cannot reach the sampler.\r\n   24: Two receipts new to the method both held: the crop-overlay check ran BEFORE\r\n   25: the panel (`CROP_OVERLAY_RECEIPT.json`), and the A/A null was receipted at\r\n   26: creation -- **97/97 frames byte-identical**\r\n   27: (`march/render/AA_CONTROL.json`), so the pipeline is bit-exact and every arm\r\n   28: difference is the knob.\r\n   29: \r\n   30: The sigma-injector ADAPT (local `_SigmasFromValues` -> registered  159: * **The A/A null was run only half-way.** `AA_CONTROL.json` proves render  174:   regions for seat 3), so per-frame flicker and any mid-clip collapse or\r\n  175:   recovery are invisible to the panel. Six side-by-side PAIR clips WERE\r\n  176:   rendered (`output/baseline_output/lane3_ltx_video/_clips/PAIR_*.mp4`) and no\r\n  177:   seat was ever given one. Lane 2's lesson was that a motion claim cannot come\r\n  178:   from stillness prompts; lane 3 fixed the stillness half and not the\r\n  179:   judged-from-stills half.\r\n  180: * **The operator's eye -- the final seat in the voted method -- was never\r\n  181:   exercised**, on this lane or on lanes 1 and 2. It cost nothing because all\r\n  182:   three closed NO WIN and a loss costs nothing downstream; it would have\r\n  183:   mattered on a WIN. The six PAIR clips on disk are exactly what an eye pass\r\n  184:   wants.\r\n  185: * Frame length was 97 against the engine's documented 169 ceiling\r\n  186:   (`_LTX_MAX_FRAMES_DEFAULT`), so a strength effect on drift or overcooking had\r\n  187:   43% less clip to accumulate in. Legal and ordinary, low materiality, recorded\r\n  188:   for completeness.\r\n  189: \r\n  190: ## Corrections and completeness -- provenance\r\n  191: \r\n  192: The completeness critic ran at lane close (one agent, per the ultracode\r\n  193: routing) and its findings above were each re-verified by the driver against\r\n  194: the real Windows files before being folded in: the margin recount, the\r\n  195: submitted-graph purity wording, the census citation, the withdrawn strip read,\r\n  196: the i2v-default bound, the byte-identical judge seats, the read-order tally,\r\n  197: and the missing panel receipts. The NCC and tone numbers were computed\r\n  198: independently by the driver from the frames on disk. **Nothing here reopens the\r\n  199: lane** -- two of these findings make the NO WIN stronger by showing the panel\r\n  200: could not have detected a win at this divergence, and one (the i2v default)\r\n  201: bounds what the null is allowed to claim.\r\n  202: \r\n  203: ## Provenance\r\n  204: \r\n  205: Workbench `basline-models`, lane `staging/lane3_ltx_video/`; frames under\r\n  206: `ComfyUI/output/baseline_output/lane3_ltx_video/`, never `otr/obs`. Panel\r\n  207: `judge/PANEL.json` (run `wf_cc532009-7af`, 18/18 seats, 0 errors -- resumed\r\n  208: across an app crash from the 17-seat journal, last seat run live). Measurement\r\n  209: only: no OTR production code, no model download, shipped recipes untouched.\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
