n  105:       \"cell\": \"officer/seed42\",\r\n  106:       \"identity_verdict\": \"HOLD\",\r\n  107:       \"maps_to\": \"TIE\",\r\n  108:       \"margin\": \"none\",\r\n  109:       \"seat\": \"seat3_crops\"\r\n  110:     },\r\n  111:     {\r\n  112:       \"basis\": \"Every countable instrument ties at full score: eye-chart row 5 legible on both panels, 3px gratings separated with exact reference bar counts, all 8 colour bars present, zero distinct hallucinated blobs - in all six frames. A wins only on tie-breaks measured from raw pixels: (1) temporal stability against the nothing-moves prompt - A's f001->f049 settle changed 11,021 px by >48 levels vs B's 21,362, with the same near-static tail after f049; (2) first-frame finest-grating contrast - 3px modulation 180/190 (L/D) for A vs 160/166 for B; (3) B carries one extra marginal smear streak under the light-panel 3px label. No count differs by even one step, and the differences are visible only at high zoom or by flipping, so the margin is marginal, not clear.\",\r\n  113:       \"better_label\": \"A\",\r\n  114:       \"cell\": \"testcard/seed20260821\",\r\n  115:       \"identity_verdict\": \"N/A\",\r\n  116:       \"maps_to\": \"soft\",\r\n  117:       \"margin\": \"marginal\",\r\n  118:       \"seat\": \"seat1_full\"\r\n  119:     },\r\n  120:     {\r\n  121:       \"basis\": \"Every countable answer is identical between the labels: both keep eye-chart rows 1-5 legible on both panels in all three frames, both hold grating separation down to the 3px group on both panels (verified by scanline modulation and bar-edge counts, not just eyeballing), both keep all 8 colour bars distinct, and neither adds a single hallucinated blob (block-diff against the 2x-upscaled reference found nothing outside the grating strip). Both exhibit the same mild one-time contrast settle between f001 and f049 and are then static. The only differences are sub-count and flip-at-zoom class: X's first frame is marginally crisper on the finest gratings (3px range 198-201 vs Y's 176-180) and its temporal settle is slightly smaller (p99 42 vs 54), while X deviates slightly more from the reference in the light 4px group at f049/f097. Since the counts are equal on every question, the honest verdict is TIE with margin none; if forced beyond the counts, X holds frame-1 fidelity marginally better, which is a MARGINAL difference by rule 5.\",\r\n  122:       \"better_label\": \"TIE\",\r\n  123:       \"cell\": \"testcard/seed20260821\",\r\n  124:       \"identity_verdict\": \"N/A\",\r\n  125:       \"maps_to\": \"TIE\",\r\n  126:       \"margin\": \"none\",\r\n  127:       \"seat\": \"seat2_full\"\r\n  128:     },\r\n  129:     {\r\n  130:       \"basis\": \"All scored counts are identical between P and Q: eye-chart rows 5/5 on both panels in both frames, gratings separated down to 3px on both panels in both frames, 0 hallucinated blobs, no qualifying inter-frame motion for either label. Q5 is UNKNOWN for every cell because no colour-bar crop was provided. The sole pixel-visible difference at native zoom is grating pitch-label text fidelity: P's dark-panel labels stay legible as the reference's 16px/12px/8px/6px in both frames, while Q's dark-panel labels are corrupted (reading roughly 15px/13px/Bpx/Epx) in both frames; light-panel labels are about equally degraded in both labels. That is a cleanliness edge to P, but a marginal one �?\" on the seven scored questions alone this is a dead tie.\",\r\n  131:       \"better_label\": \"P\",\r\n  132:       \"cell\": \"testcard/seed20260821\",\r\n  133:       \"identity_verdict\": \"N/A\",\r\n  134:       \"maps_to\": \"ours\",\r\n  135:       \"margin\": \"marginal\",\r\n  136:       \"seat\": \"seat3_crops\"\r\n  137:     },\r\n  138:     {\r\n  139:       \"basis\": \"Every asked count is identical between A and B: eye charts fully legible to row 5 on both panels in all six frames, gratings separated down to 3px on both panels in all six frames, all 8 colour bars present, zero distinct hallucinated blobs (only a faint horizontal seam across the light grating strip, present identically in both labels, not counted). Both labels answer YES on Q7 with the same character of motion: a settle between f001 and f049 (edge breathing plus visible 4px/3px grating shimmer and warping of the tiny pitch-label glyphs), then near-total stasis f049 to f097. The sole difference is drift magnitude, measured on raw pixels: A changed 30,431 px (diff>32) over f001-f049 versus B's 51,558 px, about 1.7x more drift in B; per-frame flip viewing shows this only at high zoom, so per rule 5 it is a marginal edge to A, not a clear one. TIE would also be defensible on the counted questions alone.\",\r\n  140:       \"better_label\": \"A\",\r\n  141:       \"cell\": \"testcard/seed42\",\r\n  142:       \"identity_verdict\": \"N/A\",\r\n  143:       \"maps_to\": \"soft\",\r\n  144:       \"margin\": \"marginal\",\r\n  145:       \"seat\": \"seat1_full\"\r\n  146:     },\r\n  147:     {\r\n  148:       \"basis\": \"Every countable question ties exactly: both labels hold eye-chart row 5 on light and dark panels in all three frames, resolve gratings to 3px on both panels in all frames, keep all 8 colour bars distinct, and share the same single hallucinated artifact (a faint horizontal smear band across the mid-height of the light grating strip, absent from the reference). The tiebreaker is Q7 magnitude on a nothing-moves prompt: Y's first frame is measurably softer in the fine gratings (3px column-profile modulation 168/167 light/dark vs X's 188/192) and its f001-to-f049 settle changes about twice as many pixels as X's (3.23% vs 1.91% over threshold 32; 0.57% vs 0.31% over 64), i.e. Y drifts/sharpens more before locking in; both are then statically identical f049-f097. No whole-pixel translation in either (phase correlation 0,0); the difference is visible only at high zoom or by flipping, so per the rules it is marginal, not clear.\",\r\n  149:       \"better_label\": \"X\",\r\n  150:       \"cell\": \"testcard/seed42\",\r\n  151:       \"identity_verdict\": \"N/A\",\r\n  152:       \"maps_to\": \"soft\",\r\n  153:       \"margin\": \"marginal\",\r\n  154:       \"seat\": \"seat2_full\"\r\n  155:     },\r\n  156:     {\r\n  157:       \"basis\": \"Every countable metric is equal: both labels hold full eye-chart legibility to row 5 on light and dark panels in both frames (KNORSV clearly resolved in all eight eye crops); grating stripe counts are identical (8/10/15/19/28/37 runs per band) with near-full local modulation (238-255 levels) down to the 3px band on both panels for both labels and both frames; zero hallucinated elements in any crop; and neither label shows visible inter-frame motion - a computed pixel diff between f049 and f097 finds only edge-level flicker on grating boundaries (under half a percent of pixels differing by more than 30 levels), which is not visible without differencing and is essentially the same magnitude for P and Q. The only cross-label pixel differences are slight stripe-edge phase/rendering variations in the light gratings panel, which do not change any count. Colour bars were not included in the provided crops, so Q5 is UNKNOWN for both. With every counted question tied, the honest verdict is TIE with no margin.\",\r\n  158:       \"better_label\": \"TIE\",\r\n  159:       \"cell\": \"testcard/seed42\",\r\n  160:       \"identity_verdict\": \"N/A\",\r\n  161:       \"maps_to\": \"TIE\",\r\n  162:       \"margin\": \"none\",\r\n  163:       \"seat\": \"seat3_crops\"\r\n  164:     }\r\n  165:   ],\r\n  166:   \"run\": \"wf_4d925968-580\",\r\n  167:   \"seats\": 18,\r\n  168:   \"tally\": {\r\n  169:     \"TIE\": 8,\r\n  170:     \"ours\": 4,\r\n  171:     \"soft\": 6\r\n  172:   }\r\n  173: }\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
