{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_44","type":"agent_message","text":"VERDICT: no — the lane can render, but the judging path cannot consume lane 4, the “official” loader graph omits a real input, and receipts do not bind the staged graphs, assets, or decision rule tightly enough to support a WIN.\n\nMUST-FIX BEFORE BUILD:\n\n1. [Measurement-only work / Validation & Staging Requirements] The runner targets `127.0.0.1:8000`, identified as the production headless port, and saves under the external live ComfyUI output root. That violates the required non-production staging context and repository-only write boundary (`staging/lane4_wan_text_encoder/render_arms.py:35-39,106-118`; `tools/temporal_stats.py:25`; `AGENTS.md:3-6,32-33`; `C:/Users/jeffr/Documents/ComfyUI/custom_nodes/ComfyUI-OldTimeRadio/.kibitz/comfyui.local.md:16-19`). Add required `--server`, `--input-root`, and `--output-root` arguments; run a dedicated staging ComfyUI instance on a non-production port with output/temp inside this repository; record and verify that identity before queueing.\n\n2. [Fixtures, and why these two] Lane 4 cannot reach the panel. `make_judge_set.py` has regions only for lanes 1-3 and fails any missing lane/fixture at runtime; `make_clips.py` is hard-coded to lane 1 paths, lane 1 fixture names, and an `official` candidate (`tools/make_judge_set.py:47-70,110-117`; `tools/make_clips.py:18-24,54-80`). Add explicit lane-4 support or make both tools derive lane name, arms, fixtures, output root, frame count, FPS, and blinding map from `LANE.json`/`RENDER.json`. Do not start judging until this path has a successful receipt.\n\n3. [The contrast] The “official” graph does not implement the official/core `CLIPLoader` interface as described. It omits `device: \"default\"` (`staging/lane4_wan_text_encoder/build_arms.py:51-54,126-129`; `staging/lane4_wan_text_encoder/crowd/arm_official.json:2-7`), while both the official template and OTR’s safetensors branch include that input (`C:/Users/jeffr/Documents/ComfyUI/.venv/Lib/site-packages/comfyui_workflow_templates_json/templates/video_wan2_2_5B_ti2v.json:88-91`; `C:/Users/jeffr/Documents/ComfyUI/custom_nodes/ComfyUI-OldTimeRadio/nodes/_otr_video_engines/eng_wan_ti2v.py:1005-1011`). Add the input and extend the purity model to allow a specifically declared class-required added leaf; the current unconditional `only_in_B` failure makes a faithful class swap impossible (`tools/purity_gate.py:157-166`).\n\n4. [The purity-gate change this forced] The advertised `--contrast STAGING.json` interface is incompatible with lane 4’s receipt. The gate treats every top-level `declared_contrast` member as a leaf-path expectation, but lane 4 stores `kind`, `node`, and nested `ours`/`official` objects (`tools/purity_gate.py:129-146`; `staging/lane4_wan_text_encoder/crowd/STAGING.json:6-22`). The renderer bypasses this by hard-coding class and filename expectations (`staging/lane4_wan_text_encoder/render_arms.py:132-140`). Define one versioned contrast schema containing `changed`, `added`, `removed`, and `{from,to}` class swaps; make both staging and submission gates consume it. Remove lane-specific expectation strings from the renderer.\n\n5. [The contrast / generated from the shipping engine] Rebuilding is environment-dependent but the builder does not isolate or bind that environment. OTR allows `OTR_WAN_TI2V_CLIP_NAME` and `OTR_WAN_TI2V_CLIP_LOADER` to change both the base filename and class, while `build_arms.py` only checks that the source filename is not already the official filename (`C:/Users/jeffr/Documents/ComfyUI/custom_nodes/ComfyUI-OldTimeRadio/nodes/_otr_video_engines/eng_wan_ti2v.py:634-642,703-707`; `staging/lane4_wan_text_encoder/build_arms.py:95-104`). Clear the relevant environment keys as the grounded fleet run did, then assert the exact expected base tuple: `CLIPLoaderGGUF`, Q5 filename, `type=wan`. Record the cleared/effective environment.\n\n6. [The purity-gate change this forced] Submission purity is not chained to staging purity. `build_submission` reads mutable staged files, while `gate_submissions` hashes freshly written submissions and verifies that self-generated manifest; it never checks `STAGING.json` or `LANE.json` hashes before mutation (`staging/lane4_wan_text_encoder/render_arms.py:110-141,167-194`; `staging/lane4_wan_text_encoder/crowd/STAGING.json:2-4`). Verify each staged arm against its recorded hash before adding seed/output nodes, and store both `staged_sha256` and `submitted_sha256` in every leg receipt.\n\n7. [Scope of THIS lane / Fixtures] Filenames are being treated as model and input identity. `LANE.json` and `STAGING.json` record model and image names but no content hashes (`staging/lane4_wan_text_encoder/LANE.json:2-18,30-46`; `staging/lane4_wan_text_encoder/crowd/STAGING.json:2-28`). Record resolved path, byte size, and SHA-256 for both encoders, the shared UNET/VAE, and each conditioning image; verify them immediately before and after the run. Otherwise replacing a same-named file does not invalidate the experiment.\n\n8. [Fixtures, and why these two] The proposed adherence observable is internally contradictory. The crowd role says “meter ticks,” but the positive prompt never names a meter (`staging/lane4_wan_text_encoder/build_arms.py:60-69`; `staging/lane4_wan_text_encoder/crowd/STAGING.json:28-29`). The test-card positive asks for block letters while the inherited negative explicitly suppresses “text” (`staging/lane4_wan_text_encoder/testcard_motion/arm_ours.json:69-86`). Remove unprompted meter scoring or name it explicitly; replace the test-card demand with non-conflicting attributes, or declare a shared fixture-specific negative and bound the result as non-shipping-prompt behavior.\n\n9. [Fixtures / What this plan is asking the panel, questions 2-3] Both conditioning images already contain essentially all named static content; the only novel test-card instruction is lateral motion (`C:/Users/jeffr/Documents/ComfyUI/input/lane1_crowd.png`; `C:/Users/jeffr/Documents/ComfyUI/input/lane1_testcard.png`; `staging/lane4_wan_text_encoder/build_arms.py:59-82`). The current judge harness exposes only frames 1/49/97 and fixed crops (`tools/make_judge_set.py:40-43,133-180`). [ASSUMPTION] Static preservation counts will be weakly sensitive to encoder precision because the still supplies those objects directly. Add counterfactual prompt demands absent from the still and a blinded video/trajectory seat, or drop the motion claim and label the lane unable to test encoder-specific adherence.\n\n10. [Verdict matrix] The decision rule is not executable. “Materially more,” “MORE,” “held geometry,” and “official WINS” have no field types, thresholds, tie handling, seed aggregation, or rule for conflicting fixtures (`staging/lane4_wan_text_encoder/LANE.json:48-52`). Define a panel-result schema with per-arm counts, UNKNOWN handling, structural-defect counts, motion-compliance measurements, and an exact aggregation rule. A candidate WIN should require a predeclared minimum effect replicated across both seeds, with no structural-regression veto.\n\n11. [Known open method debts] All five debts must be closed before this panel, not after. The current seat allocator flips independent digest bits rather than producing a balanced lane-wide schedule, and seats 1/2 receive the same three frames (`tools/make_judge_set.py:71-100,145-180`). For this 12-seat lane, deal exactly six candidate-first and six ours-first positions; treat duplicate full-frame seats as a reliability check excluded from voting or replace one with different evidence; compute NCC before admission; archive prompt/model/schema metadata before the first seat; and include pair clips because motion is an asserted outcome.\n\n12. [2 fixtures x 2 arms x 2 seeds] The renderer is neither idempotent nor safely resumable. A rerun starts every leg again, reuses fixed output prefixes, and rewrites `RENDER.json` from a new empty in-memory list after each leg (`staging/lane4_wan_text_encoder/render_arms.py:205-279`). It also accepts any successful frame count, assumes the first returned subfolder is authoritative, and can pass with fewer than 97 frames (`staging/lane4_wan_text_encoder/render_arms.py:247-288`). Use immutable run IDs, reject nonempty destinations, resume only legs whose graph/output hashes and exact filenames verify, require frames 1-97 exactly, and write receipts atomically.\n\n13. [Regression evidence already run] A critical shared gate change has only narrative/manual regression evidence; there is no durable test module covering the new parser and invariants (`tools/purity_gate.py:112-206`). Add automated tests for undeclared, wrong-target, phantom, duplicate, reversed-arm, added/removed class inputs, malformed declarations, literal two-item lists, wiring changes, and the lane-3 compatibility case.\n\nSHOULD-FIX:\n\n1. [The purity-gate change this forced] `_is_wire` classifies every JSON `[string, int]` as an edge without checking whether the string names a graph node (`tools/purity_gate.py:29-37`). Diffomatic already documents and avoids that literal-list ambiguity (`tools/diffomatic.py:156-173,813-827`). Make purity-gate wire detection graph-aware.\n\n2. [The contrast] `build_arms.py` prints whatever consumers it finds but does not assert that they are exactly `neg` and `pos`, slot 0 (`staging/lane4_wan_text_encoder/build_arms.py:106-110`). Assert the complete consumer set and slot before staging.\n\n3. [Error handling and failure modes] Submission catches only `HTTPError`; connection failures, invalid JSON, and a response without `prompt_id` can abort or poll `/history/None`. History polling abandons immediately on a transient `URLError` (`staging/lane4_wan_text_encoder/render_arms.py:52-62,144-164,231-245`). Add bounded retry/backoff, validate `prompt_id`, and persist a fault receipt for every failed attempt.\n\n4. [candidate_win / QUALITY TIER] No peak VRAM or model-residency data is recorded; receipts contain elapsed time and temporal statistics only (`staging/lane4_wan_text_encoder/render_arms.py:255-279`). verify: actual peak VRAM and co-residency behavior for both loaders. Reset to the same desktop/model-cache baseline, balance arm execution order, and record peak VRAM before describing a headroom threshold.\n\n5. [The contrast] Rename the treatment from “text-encoder precision” to “encoder artifact plus loader implementation.” The arm changes both stored weights and loader class (`staging/lane4_wan_text_encoder/crowd/arm_ours.json:2-7`; `staging/lane4_wan_text_encoder/crowd/arm_official.json:2-7`), so the experiment cannot attribute an effect solely to numeric precision.\n\nOPTIONAL / NICE-TO-HAVE:\n\n- Add JSON Schema validation and a schema version to `LANE.json`, `STAGING.json`, `RENDER.json`, and panel results.\n- Record per-frame hashes or a Merkle digest in `RENDER.json` and copy those hashes into judge manifests.\n- Generalize the repeated lane-specific renderer into a data-driven runner only after lane 4’s invariants are fixed.\n\nCUT THESE (over-engineering):\n\n1. [Known method debt 1] Cut `seat2_full` as an independent vote. It duplicates `seat1_full` pixels; retain it only as a consistency/noise diagnostic, which is sufficient and avoids double-counting identical evidence.\n\n2. [Fixtures] Cut static test-card acuity and lettering from the encoder verdict. Those properties are already supplied by the conditioning image, lettering conflicts with the inherited negative prompt, and the current knob-specific demand is motion.\n\n3. [candidate_win] Cut immediate “QUALITY TIER” design from this lane. A verified WIN should create one bounded OTR follow-up item; tier naming, VRAM thresholds, cross-platform compatibility, and canonical-workflow changes require separate validation and are not needed to answer this A/B."}}
